\version "2.24.0"
% RECAPITULATION, bars 151-170: theme F1 ff, fuller than at 11 (flutes and oboes on the tune from the start, trumpets and horns 3-4
% off the beat, trombones holding the harmony, tuba on the bass of the consequent). Deceptive cadence at 166 as at 26.
% c043 (form; A&S Unit 19, PDF 306, 316-317, 319-320): 151-152 the bass stays on the retransition's G under F1's head (accented, expanded cadential 6/4:
% i6/4 151, iv over the G pedal 152, V 153, V6-V4/3 154), so the thematic return (151) comes before the tonic root (155, timpani C); 11-12 have E flat-C | D-F.
% 167-170: link, VI - iiø6/5 - V6/5, diminuendo to p: the second theme in C minor follows from the inverted V (no root V-i in C).

